isor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{7}÷\\frac{2}{3s} & = \\\\ \\frac{r}{7}\\cdot \\frac{3s}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{3rs}{14} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186256994 13194139533864 true] [17592186256993 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186256993 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256993 1104 #edb/ref 17592186256994 13194139533864 true] [17592186256993 1110 #uuid "dc6fe8e4-8d27-51a6-8e50-ed3a91c11c94" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256994 1034 "\\frac{3rs}{14}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186256994 1111 #uuid "0f3ea772-6f8d-5ef8-b8a3-cdba57d45d2b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256995 1017 #edb/ref 17592186256996 13194139533864 true] [17592186256995 1089 "q-113809" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256995 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186256995 1100 "$\\frac{2{w}^{2}}{3}÷\\frac{w(w+2)}{7}=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256995 1113 #uuid "61e0aeb4-8e8b-5668-8283-bca50adbcc95" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256995 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{w}^{2}}{3}÷\\frac{w(w+2)}{7},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{w}^{2}}{3}÷\\frac{w(w+2)}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{2{w}^{2}}{3}\\cdot \\frac{7}{w(w+2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{14{w}^{2}}{3w(w+2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{14{w}^{\\cancel{2}}}{3\\cancel{w}(w+2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{14w}{3(w+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we canceled out a common factor of $w$ in the numerator and denominator." 13194139533864 true] [17592186256996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186256997 13194139533864 true] [17592186256996 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186256996 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256996 1104 #edb/ref 17592186256997 13194139533864 true] [17592186256996 1110 #uuid "222b4b13-0d63-5236-8de5-fd5b58d873b4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256997 1034 "w" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186256997 1111 #uuid "bc9f761d-8f7e-5f2e-9317-04ab8158d034" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256998 1017 #edb/ref 17592186256999 13194139533864 true] [17592186256998 1089 "q-113811" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256998 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186256998 1100 "$\\frac{{q}^{3}}{q+2}÷\\frac{{q}^{3}}{q-2}=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256998 1113 #uuid "9d7daaf2-bd4a-5a32-8a2b-83c0f24251ed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256998 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{{q}^{3}}{q+2}÷\\frac{{q}^{3}}{q-2},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{q}^{3}}{q+2}÷\\frac{{q}^{3}}{q-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{{q}^{3}}{q+2}\\cdot \\frac{q-2}{{q}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{{q}^{3}}}{q+2}\\cdot \\frac{q-2}{\\cancel{{q}^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{q-2}{q+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of ${q}^{3}$ in the numerator and denominator." 13194139533864 true] [17592186256999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257000 13194139533864 true] [17592186256999 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186256999 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186256999 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257000 13194139533864 true] [17592186256999 1110 #uuid "07a39827-8fed-5545-9f32-495415233f36" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257000 1034 "{q}^{3}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257000 1111 #uuid "c94d221a-05f5-576a-882a-bde566f30534" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257001 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257002 13194139533864 true] [17592186257001 1089 "q-113816" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257001 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257001 1100 "What is the result of dividing $\\frac{3}{5{z}^{2}}$ by $\\frac{4}{{z}^{5}}?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257001 1113 #uuid "22a6304d-13b0-5ca5-9a5d-269f6fcab12d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257001 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5{z}^{2}}÷\\frac{4}{{z}^{5}},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5{z}^{2}}÷\\frac{4}{{z}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{5{z}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{z}^{5}}{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{3{z}^{5}}{20{z}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3{z}^{3}\\cdot {z}^{2}}{20{z}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3{z}^{3}\\cdot \\cancel{{z}^{2}}}{20\\cancel{{z}^{2}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3{z}^{3}}{20} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of ${z}^{2}$ in the numerator and denominator." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257002 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257003 13194139533864 true] [17592186257002 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257002 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257002 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257003 13194139533864 true] [17592186257002 1110 #uuid "0682f16a-d826-5283-9cc4-cad7ab91344a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257003 1034 "{z}^{2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257003 1111 #uuid "6ec30f74-31b1-5239-a580-0c19575622ba" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257004 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257005 13194139533864 true] [17592186257004 1089 "q-113819" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257004 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257004 1100 "$\\frac{3rs}{7t}÷\\frac{r}{7st}=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257004 1113 #uuid "60d922f9-b9e4-5537-8b09-2f3b1f9f6f00" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257004 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{3rs}{7t}÷\\frac{r}{7st},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3rs}{7t}÷\\frac{r}{7st} & = \\\\ \\frac{3rs}{7t}\\cdot \\frac{7st}{r} & = \\\\ \\frac{3s\\cdot r}{7t}\\cdot \\frac{7t\\cdot s}{r} & = \\\\ \\frac{3s\\cdot \\cancel{r}}{\\cancel{7t}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{7t}\\cdot s}{\\cancel{r}} & = \\\\ 3{s}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257006 13194139533864 true] [17592186257005 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257005 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257005 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257006 13194139533864 true] [17592186257005 1110 #uuid "ae940c7b-ccff-532e-87d2-befe967c3621" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257006 1034 "3{s}^{2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257006 1111 #uuid "707ca36e-7efa-5fb9-9a38-6514af3cb99b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257007 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257008 13194139533864 true] [17592186257007 1089 "q-113886" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257007 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257007 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{5}\\sqrt{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257007 1113 #uuid "a8ef22d3-07d6-525f-b1e0-653bfae49fd5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257007 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\sqrt{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\sqrt{x-1},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-1}{n}=\\frac{4}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\sqrt{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{4i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{1+\\frac{4i}{n}-1}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{8}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257009 13194139533864 true] [17592186257008 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257008 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257008 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257009 13194139533864 true] [17592186257008 1110 #uuid "a5a9c9fc-6d99-5e9c-a617-fc21b7aa4cce" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257009 1034 "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{8}{n}]" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257009 1111 #uuid "b85d035c-ce66-5d55-8159-c3de5b3fe4ae" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257010 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257011 13194139533864 true] [17592186257010 1089 "q-113923" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257010 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257010 1100 "$\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}x-2\\operatorname{sec}x\\,\\operatorname{tan}x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257010 1113 #uuid "24d3110b-7801-5a06-a723-89be430fdf97" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257010 1145 "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}x-2\\operatorname{sec}x\\,\\operatorname{tan}x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\operatorname{cos}x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}x-2\\operatorname{sec}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257011 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257012 13194139533864 true] [17592186257011 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257011 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257011 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257012 13194139533864 true] [17592186257011 1110 #uuid "35c057fa-a2a6-5451-922a-284bbf17c624" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257012 1034 "3\\operatorname{sin}x-2\\operatorname{sec}x+C" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257012 1111 #uuid "7b8591f3-91f5-583e-82f0-931d29e2085e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257013 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257014 13194139533864 true] [17592186257013 1089 "q-113925" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257013 1100 "$\\int (2\\operatorname{csc}x\\,\\operatorname{cot}x+\\operatorname{sin}x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257013 1113 #uuid "4b0506f0-8883-54c9-8f52-ff9e6fd263bc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257013 1145 "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2\\operatorname{csc}x\\,\\operatorname{cot}x+\\operatorname{sin}x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\operatorname{cos}\\operatorname{csc}x\\,\\operatorname{cot}x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-\\operatorname{csc}x)+(-\\operatorname{cos}x)+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{csc}x-\\operatorname{cos}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257015 13194139533864 true] [17592186257014 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257014 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257014 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257015 13194139533864 true] [17592186257014 1110 #uuid "fce5bcac-a796-5c93-b374-510f349181dc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257015 1034 "-2\\operatorname{csc}x-\\operatorname{cos}x+C" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257015 1111 #uuid "906e9878-7fe2-5efa-800f-3b817a109a7b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257016 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257017 13194139533864 true] [17592186257016 1089 "q-113927" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257016 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257016 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257016 1113 #uuid "1804c8ea-5802-59e5-92d9-206715562863" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257016 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={e}^{x},$ the lower bound is $a=0$ and the upper bound is $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-0}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(0+k\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(\\frac{2k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[{e}^{2k/n}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257018 13194139533864 true] [17592186257017 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257017 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257017 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257018 13194139533864 true] [17592186257017 1110 #uuid "a25d2f28-6227-5300-8084-fcf842ad6d18" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257018 1034 "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[{e}^{2k/n}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257018 1111 #uuid "9282bab5-deb0-5c96-8746-c1502da05608" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257019 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257020 13194139533864 true] [17592186257019 1089 "q-113935" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257019 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257019 1100 "$\\int -\\frac{3}{2}{sec}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257019 1113 #uuid "292b56dc-de2a-5032-a17e-6e3b6f3c4acc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257019 1145 "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int {sec}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{tan}x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{3}{2}{sec}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {sec}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{tan}x)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{tan}x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257020 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257021 13194139533864 true] [17592186257020 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257020 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257020 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257021 13194139533864 true] [17592186257020 1110 #uuid "bb3748a2-26ac-5a77-9f78-65aafdcf23fa" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257021 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{tan}x+C" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257021 1111 #uuid "39a1f50a-60e1-5466-b4f7-e006aef3faca" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257022 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257023 13194139533864 true] [17592186257022 1089 "q-113941" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257022 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257022 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257022 1113 #uuid "23c94ac6-51bf-5545-8513-402f0a143fe8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257022 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\sqrt{x},$ the lower bound is $a=4$ and the upper bound is $b=9.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{9-4}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(4+k\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(4+\\frac{5k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{4+\\frac{5k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257023 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257024 13194139533864 true] [17592186257023 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257023 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257023 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257024 13194139533864 true] [17592186257023 1110 #uuid "db4bf4bc-7f65-51e5-a960-8db46f7bb8d9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257024 1034 "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{4+\\frac{5k}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257024 1111 #uuid "cbded5ce-14f9-54a9-9b89-593da772eac3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257025 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257026 13194139533864 true] [17592186257025 1089 "q-113948" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257025 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257025 1100 "$\\int -\\frac{5}{2}{csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257025 1113 #uuid "bb1ca69c-b1be-58c9-acc5-e85cafc81f4d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257025 1145 "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cot}x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{5}{2}{csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}(-\\operatorname{cot}x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257026 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257027 13194139533864 true] [17592186257026 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257026 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257026 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257027 13194139533864 true] [17592186257026 1110 #uuid "d901ddfb-d381-5f54-bb31-d22d40e9b945" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257027 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}x+C" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257027 1111 #uuid "97108131-e84b-5240-bd86-678584456dfc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257028 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257029 13194139533864 true] [17592186257028 1089 "q-113952" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257028 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257028 1100 "$\\int 3{csc}^{2}x-4\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257028 1113 #uuid "2a9755d5-7b55-50ff-b000-477adfea203f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257028 1145 "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}x+C, \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cot}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{csc}^{2}x-4\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int {csc}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int \\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(-\\operatorname{cot}x)-4(\\operatorname{sec}x)+C \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cot}x-4\\operatorname{sec}x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257029 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257030 13194139533864 true] [17592186257029 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257029 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257029 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257030 13194139533864 true] [17592186257029 1110 #uuid "0bbb2e46-f019-593f-8d30-76e2e4fa2ace" 13194139533864 tru