uid "a11523de-e56f-519e-9942-a7970fdb93f2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257034 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257035 13194139533864 true] [17592186257034 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257037 13194139533864 true] [17592186257034 1089 "q-113962" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257034 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257034 1100 "Find the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(2c,-d)$ and $(6c,6d).$\n\nCoordinate 1: {{coordinate-1}}\n\nCoordinate 2: {{coordinate-2}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257034 1113 #uuid "b1b6dcd8-b86b-57fe-bcef-873b76734928" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257034 1145 "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(2c,-d)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(6c,6d)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2c+6c}{2},\\frac{-d+6d}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8c}{2},\\frac{5d}{2}) \\\\  & =(4c,\\frac{5d}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257036 13194139533864 true] [17592186257035 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257035 1041 "coordinate-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257035 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257036 13194139533864 true] [17592186257035 1110 #uuid "e4b4d01d-0a3e-55dd-8bb1-80e8e50310d9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257036 1034 "4c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257036 1111 #uuid "f01617ca-9501-5b8a-82c2-89d9dc47e19e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257038 13194139533864 true] [17592186257037 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257037 1041 "coordinate-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257037 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257038 13194139533864 true] [17592186257037 1110 #uuid "76722a3b-6111-5612-be4f-fa0048eb8261" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257038 1034 "\\frac{5d}{2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257038 1111 #uuid "158bf710-9ae8-5ca9-a8a3-0069a5332089" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257039 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257040 13194139533864 true] [17592186257039 1089 "q-114085" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257039 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257039 1100 "If $\\frac{14{p}^{5}}{5{r}^{4}}\\cdot X=\\frac{7{p}^{2}}{10{r}^{3}},$ then what is $X?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257039 1113 #uuid "2a05ba22-ceea-515c-a875-0a403f6eecc1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257039 1145 "Since $\\frac{14{p}^{5}}{5{r}^{4}}\\cdot X=\\frac{7{p}^{2}}{10{r}^{3}},$ we have\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{7{p}^{2}}{10{r}^{3}}÷\\frac{14{p}^{5}}{5{r}^{4}}.\n$$\n\nTo compute this quotient, we just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{p}^{2}}{10{r}^{3}}÷\\frac{14{p}^{5}}{5{r}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7{p}^{2}}{10{r}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{5{r}^{4}}{14{p}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7{p}^{2}}{2\\cdot 5{r}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{5{r}^{3}\\cdot r}{2\\cdot 7{p}^{2}\\cdot {p}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7{p}^{2}}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{5{r}^{3}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{5{r}^{3}}\\cdot r}{2\\cdot \\cancel{7{p}^{2}}\\cdot {p}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{r}{2{p}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{r}{4{p}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257041 13194139533864 true] [17592186257040 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257040 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257040 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257041 13194139533864 true] [17592186257040 1110 #uuid "12651517-3871-5729-91f9-1d7a5b577ef7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257041 1034 "\\frac{r}{4{p}^{3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257041 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257041 1111 #uuid "b978cdde-56b3-5b60-86cf-6956cdd05c3a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257042 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257043 13194139533864 true] [17592186257042 1089 "q-114088" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257042 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257042 1100 "If $\\frac{(p+5)^{2}}{18{w}^{2}}\\cdot X=\\frac{(p+5)^{3}}{4{w}^{3}},$ then what is $X?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257042 1113 #uuid "1b5af612-e59b-568d-b2ca-d0e796933c27" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257042 1145 "Since $\\frac{(p+5)^{2}}{18{w}^{2}}\\cdot X=\\frac{(p+5)^{3}}{4{w}^{3}},$ we have\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{(p+5)^{3}}{4{w}^{3}}÷\\frac{(p+5)^{2}}{18{w}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo compute this quotient, we just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(p+5)^{3}}{4{w}^{3}}÷\\frac{(p+5)^{2}}{18{w}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(p+5)^{3}}{4{w}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{18{w}^{2}}{(p+5)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(p+5)^{2}\\cdot (p+5)}{2{w}^{2}\\cdot 2w}\\cdot \\frac{9\\cdot 2{w}^{2}}{(p+5)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{(p+5)^{2}}\\cdot (p+5)}{\\cancel{2{w}^{2}}\\cdot 2w}\\cdot \\frac{9\\cdot \\cancel{2{w}^{2}}}{\\cancel{(p+5)^{2}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(p+5)}{2w}\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ \\frac{9(p+5)}{2w}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257044 13194139533864 true] [17592186257043 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257043 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257043 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257044 13194139533864 true] [17592186257043 1110 #uuid "7542b50d-4c59-5498-8591-3fc12674cea5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257044 1034 "\\frac{9(p+5)}{2w}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257044 1111 #uuid "159c5924-3709-5f54-9832-a1a69f42ddf8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257046 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257048 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257050 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1089 "q-114105" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1100 "Find the roots of the polynomial $p(m)=12{m}^{3}-40{m}^{2}+32m.$\n\nValue 1 (least to greatest): {{root-1}}\n\nValue 2 (least to greatest): {{root-2}}\n\nValue 3 (least to greatest): {{root-3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1113 #uuid "3ccdcefc-3859-5e5e-b654-0942c0cd9b0a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257045 1145 "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(m)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n12{m}^{3}-40{m}^{2}+32m=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $4m.$ We can factor out the $4m$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4m(3{m}^{2}-10m+8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $3{m}^{2}-10m+8$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4m(3{m}^{2}-10m+8) & =0 \\\\ 4m(3m-4)(m-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $m=0,$ $m=\\frac{4}{3},$ and $m=2.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257046 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257047 13194139533864 true] [17592186257046 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257046 1041 "root-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257046 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257047 13194139533864 true] [17592186257046 1110 #uuid "3c683ed6-44dd-5ec1-bbef-331b725c8d2f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257047 1034 "0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257047 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257047 1111 #uuid "ae348432-0720-5583-9a0c-2a85d61b6bfe" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257049 13194139533864 true] [17592186257048 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257048 1041 "root-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257048 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257049 13194139533864 true] [17592186257048 1110 #uuid "e7fcbcc6-b4c6-57b1-8d75-221f1352fabf" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257049 1034 "\\frac43" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257049 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257049 1111 #uuid "3039bd7e-8aad-56e7-b4fe-48843b2328cc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257050 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257051 13194139533864 true] [17592186257050 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257050 1041 "root-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257050 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257051 13194139533864 true] [17592186257050 1110 #uuid "8299e1c2-d413-5837-adf9-d8296c55ea50" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257051 1034 "2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257051 1111 #uuid "9615aa38-22ea-5d87-8582-789481a72002" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257053 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257055 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257057 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1089 "q-114111" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1100 "If $3{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-4{h}^{3}=16{h}^{3}-13{h}^{5},$ then what are the values of $h?$\n\nValue 1 (least to greatest): {{root-1}}\n\nValue 2 (least to greatest): {{root-2}}\n\nValue 3 (least to greatest): {{root-3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1113 #uuid "88e36ae1-6e90-5316-b5dc-6894542c0206" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257052 1145 "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(t)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-4{h}^{3} & =16{h}^{3}-13{h}^{5} \\\\ 16{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-4{h}^{3} & =16{h}^{3} \\\\ 16{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-20{h}^{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $4{h}^{3}.$ We can factor out the $4{h}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-20{h}^{3} & =0 \\\\ 4{h}^{3}(4{h}^{2}-8h-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $4{h}^{2}-8h-5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{h}^{3}(4{h}^{2}-8h-5) & =0 \\\\ 4{h}^{3}(2h+1)(2h-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $h=0,$ $h=-\\frac{1}{2},$ and $h=\\frac{5}{2}.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257053 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257054 13194139533864 true] [17592186257053 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257053 1041 "root-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257053 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257054 13194139533864 true] [17592186257053 1110 #uuid "0f20be64-0e50-5b43-bf6e-f9001d0ec481" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257054 1034 "-\\frac12" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257054 1111 #uuid "45c68f0d-8058-5860-98e5-666578dbc6dc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257056 13194139533864 true] [17592186257055 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257055 1041 "root-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257055 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257056 13194139533864 true] [17592186257055 1110 #uuid "f8f075eb-6bae-5f80-97fa-363137787ff6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257056 1034 "0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257056 1111 #uuid "f2a28a2b-3f64-5f43-9d8b-9c51a6558d42" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257058 13194139533864 true] [17592186257057 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257057 1041 "root-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257057 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257058 13194139533864 true] [17592186257057 1110 #uuid "b2d0a772-5867-524f-8afa-c289daddb092" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257058 1034 "\\frac52" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257058 1111 #uuid "71b3863a-c1be-59af-9b90-eec48e7c1ea2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257060 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257062 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257064 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1089 "q-114145" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1100 "Solve ${m}^{3}-3{m}^{2}-2m+6=0.$\n\nValue 1 (least to greatest): {{root-1}}\n\nValue 2 (least to greatest): {{root-2}}\n\nValue 3 (least to greatest): {{root-3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1113 #uuid "a4c3b57b-4f7f-5532-bd9e-228bcbf5fb45" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257059 1145 "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{3}-3{m}^{2}-2m+6 & = \\\\ ({m}^{3}-3{m}^{2})-(2m-6) & = \\\\ {m}^{2}(m-3)-2(m-3) & = \\\\ (m-3)\\cdot {m}^{2}-(m-3)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (m-3)({m}^{2}-2) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(m-3)({m}^{2}-2)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(m-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m-3 & =0 \\\\ m & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({m}^{2}-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ {m}^{2} & =2 \\\\ m & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=3,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257060 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257061 13194139533864 true] [17592186257060 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257060 1041 "root-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257060 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257061 13194139533864 true] [17592186257060 1110 #uuid "8af7d4f7-3b32-5c18-a8eb-978ee876b78b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257061 1034 "-\\sqrt2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257061 1111 #uuid "1bb58f1b-ad77-5cae-90c8-ea9646ffaddb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257063 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1041 "root-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257063 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1110 #uuid "ea22afb8-c570-5fdb-8e76-29ae379540b9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1034 "\\sqrt2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1111 #uuid "61aec294-9680-5eee-a1e6-d30e05f7dc5f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257065 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1041 "root-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257065 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1110 #uuid "b1df33b5-cfb0-5844-9815-e3e3017e433a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257065 1034 "3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257065 1111 #uuid "e7fce91d-b78d-5daa-9eed-3799c8e24a06" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257067 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257069 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257071 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1089 "q-114205" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1100 "Solve $-18{v}^{3}-63{v}^{2}+2v+7=0.$\n\nValue 1 (least to greatest): {{root-1}}\n\nValue 2 (least to greatest): {{root-2}}\n\nValue 3 (least to greatest): {{root-3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1113 #uuid "a3c48b1d-9c5d-5b27-89de-0584bf82834b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1145 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\n18{v}^{3}+63{v}^{2}-2v-7=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18{v}^{3}+63{v}^{2}-2v-7 & = \\\\ 9{v}^{2}(2v+7)-1(2v+7) & = \\\\ (9{v}^{2}-1)(2v+7) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(9{v}^{2}-1)(2v+7)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(9{v}^{2}-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{v}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {v}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ v & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2v+7)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v & =-7 \\\\ v & =-\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $v=-\\frac{7}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257068 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1041 "root-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257068 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1110 #uuid "3a584ce7-9315-5a23-b80e-2605fbf76445" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257068 1034 "-\\frac72" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257068 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257068 1111 #uuid "3d4fdd28-7877-56a4-bc70-4e8b10186cde" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257070 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1041 "root-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257070 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1110 #uuid "641d8c63-1219-58d4-8e45-b974fdb2de65" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1034 "-\\frac13" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1111 #uuid "da0fccf8-c278-5e86-9eed-d7be58b2c9e8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257072 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1041 "root-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257072 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1110 #uuid "bca6de13-e11f-58a0-a5da-a5be6ab24e19" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257072 1034 "\\frac13" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257072 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257072 1111 #uuid "0628c3c7-35d3-534e-b42d-73e3db0b2732" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257074 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1089 "q-114209" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1100 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{3}{1+{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\text{d}t=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1113 #uuid "9e33d82b-67b7-5f1d-84c4-6afcc46ec7f6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1145 "We split the integral into the sum of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{3}{1+{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}t\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{arctan}1-\\operatorname{arctan}0)+\\frac{1}{3}({1}^{3}-{0}^{1}) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0)+\\frac{1}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi +4}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257075 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257075 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1110 #uuid "b703f3c5-9f22-567a-aa37-1280b069e67d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1034 "\\frac{9\\pi +4}{12}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1111 #uuid "57a6ab14-c083-5397-b5c0-92247b539573" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257077 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257079 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257081 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1089 "q-114210" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1100 "Solve $-{m}^{3}-3{m}^{2}+25m+75=0.$\n\nValue 1 (least to greatest): {{root-1}}\n\nValue 2 (least to greatest): {{root-2}}\n\nValue 3 (least to greatest): {{root-3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1113 #uuid "62a71b17-2204-59c1-8d38-eaaccf24e868" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1145 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\n{m}^{3}+3{m}^{2}-25m-75=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{3}+3{m}^{2}-25m-75 & = \\\\ ({m}^{3}+3{m}^{2})+(-25m-75) & = \\\\ {m}^{2}(m+3)-25(m+3) & = \\\\ ({m}^{2}-25)(m+3) & = \\\\ (m+5)(m-5)(m+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(m+5)(m-5)(m+3)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(m+5)$ equal to $0,$ we get $m=-5.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(m-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get $m=5.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(m+3)$ equal to $0,$ we get $m=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=-3,\\,\\pm 5.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257078 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1041 "root-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257078 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1110 #uuid "f6d70c21-c5c7-5a91-ad70-3da57be7affc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1034 "-5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1111 #uuid "e472f6af-282c-5f81-8a6f-aa842163264c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257080 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1041 "root-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257080 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1110 #uuid "e4280d61-9ff1-5d9c-a021-b2720a3231c9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257080 1034 "-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257080 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257080 1111 #uuid "38e65078-5b50-50dd-8580-957b11fe5c19" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257082 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1041 "root-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257082 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1110 #uuid "771c2df9-b495-5230-a083-074b60a82938" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1034 "5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1111 #uuid "01c18fee-8168-5be8-b443-ccc5b402231c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257084 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1089 "q-114253" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1100 "${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-6x+9}{8\\sqrt{x+1}-2x-10}=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1113 #uuid "35cad922-9f73-5ba1-b352-62472240f419" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1145 "If we plug in $x=3$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-6x+9}{8\\sqrt{x+1}-2x-10} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{[{x}^{2}-6x+9]}^{'}}{[8\\sqrt{x+1}-2x-10]^{'}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{2x-6}{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{2(x+1)^{-1/2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-6x+9}{8\\sqrt{x+1}-2x-10} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x-3}{2(x+1)^{-1/2}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{[x-3]}^{'}}{[2(x+1)^{-1/2}-1]^{'}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{1}{-(x+1)^{-3/2}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 3}(x+1)^{3/2} \\\\  & =-(3+1)^{3/2} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257085 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257085 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1110 #uuid "a8edd50f-599e-5978-9f52-899e36acd0e2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1034 "-8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1111 #uuid "45048763-18a9-5264-ab1c-dabdb5d833c2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257087 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257089 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257091 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1089 "q-114339" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1100 "Solve $8{u}^{3}-6{u}^{2}-72u+54=0.$\n\nValue 1 (least to greatest): {{root-1}}\n\nValue 2 (least to greatest): {{root-2}}\n\nValue 3 (least to greatest): {{root-3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1113 #uuid "a79ebad8-83ac-5875-bf1f-d77b87643be1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1145 "Since we have an overall common factor of $2$, we start by dividing our equation through by $2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2}-36u+27=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we factor by grouping. Notice that when grouping the smaller terms, we factor out the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2}-36u+27 & = \\\\ (4{u}^{3}-3{u}^{2})-(36u-27) & = \\\\ {u}^{2}(4u-3)-9(4u-3) & = \\\\ (4u-3)\\cdot {u}^{2}-(4u-3)\\cdot 9 & = \\\\ (4u-3)({u}^{2}-9) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set each factor equal to $0$ and solve:\n\n- Setting the factor $(4u-3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-3 & =0 \\\\ 4u & =3 \\\\ u & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({u}^{2}-9)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2} & =9 \\\\ u & =\\pm 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions to the given equation are $\\frac{3}{4}$ and $\\pm 3.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257088 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1041 "root-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257088 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1110 #uuid "92d6932f-6710-5414-aa49-fb7f88f2cad2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257088 1034 "-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257088 1103 #edb/ref 175921860