ta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257553 13194139533864 true] [17592186257552 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257552 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257552 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257553 13194139533864 true] [17592186257552 1110 #uuid "50d51e71-0b6e-565a-af8e-cbcc29f8d9ed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257553 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257553 1111 #uuid "dcc56e73-6d91-5260-9a54-6114bd81cda1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257554 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257555 13194139533864 true] [17592186257554 1089 "q-123754" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257554 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257554 1100 "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=t-4,\\,\\,\\,y=1-2{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t\\le 4,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $b$ | $c$ | $-31$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257554 1113 #uuid "c56dbdf4-b093-5a0b-896e-fd12c3e29f0f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257554 1145 "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=t-4.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=0-4=-4.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=1-2{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=1-2(2)^{2}=-7.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=1-2{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=1-2(3)^{2}=-17\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+(-7)+(-17)=-28.\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257556 13194139533864 true] [17592186257555 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257555 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257555 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257556 13194139533864 true] [17592186257555 1110 #uuid "8884e2e3-45f2-59ba-a7ec-06e8f55db610" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257556 1034 "-28" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257556 1111 #uuid "6b56962b-255e-51b5-8b0e-4c1c7dd1a168" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257557 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257558 13194139533864 true] [17592186257557 1089 "q-123830" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257557 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257557 1100 "Given that  ${a}_{n}=(2n)!$ for $n\\ge 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - $\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}\\ge 1$ for all $n\\ge 1$\nII. - ${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence\nIII. - ${a}_{n}$ is a decreasing sequence" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257557 1113 #uuid "f7a7813f-e804-5d6c-b87c-980e27be4a3f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257557 1145 "Suppose the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is a positive sequence defined for $n\\ge 1,$ and that\n\n$$\nL=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- if $L\\ge 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *increasing,* and\n\n- if $0<L\\le 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *decreasing.*\n\nNotice that, in this case, ${a}_{n}=(2n)!$ is positive for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the ratio $L,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}} & =\\frac{(2(n+1))!}{(2n)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2n+2)!}{(2n)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2n+2)\\cdot (2n+1)\\cdot (2n)!}{(2n)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2n+2)\\cdot (2n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{(2n)!}}{\\cancel{(2n)!}} \\\\  & =(2n+2)(2n+1) \\\\  & \\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement III is false. Since $L\\ge 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ we can conclude that the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is increasing.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257559 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257560 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257561 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257562 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257563 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257564 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257565 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257566 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257564 13194139533864 true] [17592186257558 1110 #uuid "4f5fc15e-4bd1-594d-bf6e-a168bad9446a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257559 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257559 1111 #uuid "5ff178ed-6078-51ef-856c-8ebc0495c4b4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257560 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257560 1111 #uuid "21b232e0-03f7-5eb2-adc6-bb5e6cb9d78d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257561 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257561 1111 #uuid "91faf9c1-42f4-57e9-9402-e0d79ddb9734" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257562 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257562 1111 #uuid "638f9b90-82b1-5356-974f-1720d2deaa40" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257563 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257563 1111 #uuid "716c0bd5-9251-5471-a449-007d2dc88bfd" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257564 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257564 1111 #uuid "70344720-f832-5ba3-8f40-b16f255ae8af" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257565 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257565 1111 #uuid "1b320a43-ad5c-5dfd-a41b-e516802b30e2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257566 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257566 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257566 1111 #uuid "aff5b700-74f3-5b4e-bcf9-ebfb3c1f41d8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257567 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257568 13194139533864 true] [17592186257567 1089 "q-123832" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257567 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257567 1100 "Given that  ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n!}$ for $n\\ge 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - $\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}\\ge 1$ for all $n\\ge 1$\nII. - ${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence\nIII. - ${a}_{n}$ is a decreasing sequence" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257567 1113 #uuid "fa300e70-1aa0-5ea9-b533-c6999af1ac96" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257567 1145 "Suppose the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is a positive sequence defined for $n\\ge 1,$ and that\n\n$$\nL=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- if $L\\ge 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *increasing,* and\n\n- if $0<L\\le 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *decreasing.*\n\nNotice that, in this case, ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n!}$ is positive for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the ratio $L,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}} & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{(n+1)!})}{(\\frac{1}{n!})} \\\\  & =\\frac{n!}{(n+1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{n!}{(n+1)\\cdot n!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{n!}}{(n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{n!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n+1} \\\\  & \\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false whereas statement III is true. Since $0\\le L<1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ we can conclude that the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257569 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257570 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257571 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257572 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257573 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257574 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257575 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257576 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257573 13194139533864 true] [17592186257568 1110 #uuid "9c7ec8b4-0a9b-5fcb-8280-de4e086351ae" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257569 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257569 1111 #uuid "fa0a5f21-9f8a-53dc-b0af-1115d94652c5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257570 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257570 1111 #uuid "f3351e5e-3f56-53c9-9626-6bb7e6254fae" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257571 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257571 1111 #uuid "4278e55e-54fe-5930-8a6a-b24bf10e09d5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257572 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257572 1111 #uuid "14576f93-39d1-5d0a-a612-b13bf42e327d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257573 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257573 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257573 1111 #uuid "9ec29120-1aca-50bf-941f-8666b49457ff" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257574 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257574 1111 #uuid "f25d0059-9c21-538f-8182-201fc33118a4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257575 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257575 1111 #uuid "6b58ed57-564c-5fe2-befc-bbf155dfce35" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257576 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257576 1111 #uuid "2344dd6a-b951-57d9-8959-b149dabbc625" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257577 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257578 13194139533864 true] [17592186257577 1089 "q-123940" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257577 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257577 1100 "Find the eleventh partial sum of the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(2-2n).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257577 1113 #uuid "66d6f0cd-ec5e-58d6-b37c-1dc9aefebc12" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257577 1145 "Let ${a}_{n}=2-2n.$ If we compute the first few terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2-2(1)=0 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2-2(2)=-2 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2-2(3)=-4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we notice that this is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=-2$ and first term ${a}_{1}=0.$ \n\nWe can compute the $k$th partial sum of an arithmetic series using the formula\n\n$$\n{s}_{k}=\\frac{k}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{k}).\n$$\n\nSince ${a}_{11}=2-2(11)=-20,$ we get\n\n$$\n{s}_{11}=\\frac{11}{2}(0-20)=-110.\n$$\n\nSo the eleventh partial sum of ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(2-2n)$ is equal to $-110.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257578 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257579 13194139533864 true] [17592186257578 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257578 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257578 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257579 13194139533864 true] [17592186257578 1110 #uuid "1b400207-bef6-55aa-8972-5e014ca89499" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257579 1034 "-110" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257579 1111 #uuid "2c354b3b-46f8-52ed-b64b-3bd9ce8ee2eb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257580 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257581 13194139533864 true] [17592186257580 1089 "q-123946" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257580 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257580 1100 "Find the $k$th partial sum of the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-2n).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257580 1113 #uuid "1eaf8363-468f-5d8e-a0bf-40b4da507827" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257580 1145 "Let ${a}_{n}=-2n.$ If we compute the first few terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =-2(1)=-2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-2(2)=-4 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-2(3)=-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we see that this is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=-2$ and ${a}_{1}=-2.$ \n\nWe can compute the $k$th partial sum of an arithmetic series using the formula\n\n$$\n{s}_{k}=\\frac{k}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{k}).\n$$\n\nSince ${a}_{k}=-2k$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{k} & =\\frac{k}{2}(-2+(-2k)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{k(2+2k)}{2} \\\\  & =-k(1+k).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257582 13194139533864 true] [17592186257581 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257581 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257581 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257582 13194139533864 true] [17592186257581 1110 #uuid "06e08717-22ce-5e3d-8f3d-8d563bc237e8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257582 1034 "-k(1+k)" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257582 1111 #uuid "fe07d2f2-a8b3-5d12-b95b-fba8dbab9c78" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257583 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257584 13194139533864 true] [17592186257583 1089 "q-123947" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257583 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257583 1100 "Find the $k$th partial sum of the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(2-3n).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257583 1113 #uuid "88a08d4f-2fec-5f88-b2ca-6305b4e3802f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257583 1145 "Let ${a}_{n}=2-3n.$ If we compute the first few terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2-3(1)=-1 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2-3(3)=-7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we see that this is an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=-3$ and ${a}_{1}=-1.$ \n\nWe can compute the $k$th partial sum of an arithmetic series using the formula\n\n$$\n{s}_{k}=\\frac{k}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{k}).\n$$\n\nSince ${a}_{k}=2-3k$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{k} & =\\frac{k}{2}(-1+(2-3k)) \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}(1-3k) \\\\  & =\\frac{k(1-3k)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257585 13194139533864 true] [17592186257584 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257584 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257584 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257585 13194139533864 true] [17592186257584 1110 #uuid "cb85ead7-ad6d-5eb5-ae2b-cddb4a29e87f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257585 1034 "\\frac{k(1-3k)}{2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257585 1111 #uuid "636ed161-bef0-57c9-bfc5-0998f85dc473" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257587 13194139533864 true] [17592186257586 1089 "q-123953" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257586 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257586 1100 "Determine the third partial sum of the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{n}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257586 1113 #uuid "08572949-7072-5fd4-8efb-71e1ae8b0ef7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257586 1145 "Let ${a}_{n}={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{n}.$ We note that this is a geometric sequence with $r=\\frac{3}{4}$ and first term given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe $k$th partial sum of a geometric series is given by\n\n$$\n{s}_{k}={a}_{1}(\\frac{1-{r}^{k}}{1-r}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third partial sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{3}={\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot \\frac{(1-{r}^{3})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{(1-{[\\frac{3}{4}]}^{3})}{(1-\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{(1-\\frac{27}{64})}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}}\\cdot \\frac{(\\frac{37}{64})}{(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{111}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257588 13194139533864 true] [17592186257587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257587 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257588 13194139533864 true] [17592186257587 1110 #uuid "b47e73b7-93d8-592f-8c7f-093290c1c619" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257588 1034 "\\frac{111}{64}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257588 1111 #uuid "1dcbcdb3-5e2f-56b9-bcfa-9b3fa533e8a2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257589 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257590 13194139533864 true] [17592186257589 1089 "q-123961" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257589 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257589 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\sqrt{3}).$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257589 1113 #uuid "743b96cc-15a3-5525-bc3d-b9c616d0fdc1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257589 1145 "Let's compute the first few partial sums:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{1} & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {s}_{2} & =-\\sqrt{3}+(-\\sqrt{3})=-2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {s}_{3} & =-\\sqrt{3}+(-\\sqrt{3})+(-\\sqrt{3})=-3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {s}_{4} & =-\\sqrt{3}+(-\\sqrt{3})+(-\\sqrt{3})+(-\\sqrt{3})=-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the sequence of partial sums, we can see that the formula for the $n$th partial sum is \n\n$$\n{s}_{n}=-\\sqrt{3}n.\n$$\n\nThe sequence of partial sums is divergent:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{s}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(-\\sqrt{3}n)=-\\infty \n$$\n\nTherefore, the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\sqrt{3})$ is also divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257591 13194139533864 true] [17592186257590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257592 13194139533864 true] [17592186257590 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257590 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257590 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257591 13194139533864 true] [17592186257590 1110 #uuid "97963b45-365e-5cfd-b622-26978b6bae07" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257591 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257591 1111 #uuid "7b01190d-f335-5a2f-9c2f-a1d6a06a1693" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257592 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257592 1111 #uuid "75282ae4-fa28-5274-b61f-5ff217fb2b6f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257594 13194139533864 true] [17592186257593 1089 "q-123969" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257593 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257593 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ).$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257593 1113 #uuid "07ca5e2d-77a2-57ef-9113-ced1d4775a46" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257593 1145 "Let's compute the first few partial sums:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{1} & =\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1 \\\\ {s}_{2} & =-1+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})=0 \\\\ {s}_{3} & =0+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{7\\pi }{2})=-1 \\\\ {s}_{4} & =-1+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{9\\pi }{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we can see that the sequence of partial sums oscillates between $0$ and $-1$ forever. \n\nSo the limit of the sequence of partial sums does not exist, and therefore the series is divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257595 13194139533864 true] [17592186257594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257596 13194139533864 true] [17592186257594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257594 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257595 13194139533864 true] [17592186257594 1110 #uuid "fc98c227-8f2c-5b60-8bb3-540c6f306dcc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257595 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257595 1111 #uuid "a66ce1c5-7ce5-5c02-afed-46f3d17ce2e7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257596 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257596 1111 #uuid "522c1f8e-78bc-58fa-9df4-84520078285a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257597 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257598 13194139533864 true] [17592186257597 1089 "q-124060" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257597 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257597 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{n}{2}.$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257597 1113 #uuid "c556c0fb-0999-5d66-8c7d-1dbc40d7dbff" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257597 1145 "The given series is an arithmetic series. Its first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nand its $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{n}{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we get the following formula for the $n$th partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{n} & =\\frac{n}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{n}) \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{n}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{n(1+n)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTaking the limit of the partial sums, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{s}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n(1+n)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{n}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the limit of the sequence of partial sums is infinite, the series is divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257599 13194139533864 true] [17592186257598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257600 13194139533864 true] [17592186257598 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257598 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257598 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257599 13194139533864 true] [17592186257598 1110 #uuid "b69e70c1-efa4-5882-aa08-8ecc147d051d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257599 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257599 1111 #uuid "8d67d966-acfc-5538-936e-5bb90e6f6882" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257600 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257600 1111 #uuid "a3688785-1084-5422-8f3a-12fc901bf9f4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257601 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257602 13194139533864 true] [17592186257601 1089 "q-124062" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257601 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257601 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(n+3).$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257601 1113 #uuid "afd7d27e-c371-5649-a501-b00a45a6a8b4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257601 1145 "The given series is an arithmetic series. Its first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1+3=4,\n$$\n\nIts $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=n+3.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we get the following formula for the $n$th partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{n} & =\\frac{n}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{n}) \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{2}(4+n+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{n(7+n)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTaking the limit of the partial sums, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{s}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n(7+n)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{n}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the limit of the sequence of partial sums is infinite, the series is divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257603 13194139533864 true] [17592186257602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257604 13194139533864 true] [17592186257602 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257602 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257602 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257603 13194139533864 true] [17592186257602 1110 #uuid "5291b67e-7185-5f08-96fc-2f36ec0b9d6d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257603 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257603 1111 #uuid "db8ae490-21a6-564a-8c12-32e6bd7fc5f5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257604 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257604 1111 #uuid "16877732-d7c6-5ba5-a177-69fec44dad3f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257605 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257606 13194139533864 true] [17592186257605 1089 "q-124064" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257605 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257605 1100 "If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}=-\\frac{3}{4}$, \nthen calculate ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{a}_{n}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257605 1113 #uuid "8c0a953b-56c6-5668-952a-c90e6b1ea708" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257605 1145 "Taking the constant factor outside of the summation sign gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{a}_{n} & =8{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n} \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257607 13194139533864 true] [17592186257606 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257606 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257606 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257607 13194139533864 true] [17592186257606 1110 #uuid "83199529-9873-5d3d-9f07-29285488bb05" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257607 1034 "-6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257607 1111 #uuid "42142022-6da5-5db6-96e0-957c33de6428" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257608 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257609 13194139533864 true] [17592186257608 1089 "q-124072" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257608 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257608 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, determine all real values of $K$ for which ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(1-K)\\cdot {a}_{n}$ is divergent.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257608 1113 #uuid "3facbd4e-9556-5051-9eb1-216d555a418e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257608 1145 "If we multiply the terms of a divergent series by a non-zero constant, the resulting series is divergent.\n\nTherefore, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(1-K)\\cdot {a}_{n}\n$$\n\nis divergent when\n\n$$\n1-K\\ne 0\\,\\Rightarrow \\,K\\ne 1.\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257610 13194139533864 true] [17592186257609 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257609 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257609 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257610 13194139533864 true] [17592186257609 1110 #uuid "1538003d-0c56-57eb-b9d4-0240798a4933" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257610 1034 "1-K\\ne 0\\,\\Rightarrow \\,K\\ne 1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257610 1111 #uuid "9fb046bf-0e86-518e-9e56-3a39bf560af0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257611 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257612 13194139533864 true] [17592186257611 1089 "q-124085" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257611 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257611 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, which of the following statements is true regarding the series ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n},$ where $k$ is a positive integer, and ${a}_{n}$ is well-defined for all $n⩾1?$\n\nI. - It is convergent for $1<k\\le 500$\nII. - It is divergent for $k>500$\nIII. - It is convergent for $50<k\\le 100$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257611 1113 #uuid "f70941eb-1b43-57e6-9bb7-b412bbea5880" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257611 1145 "Removing the first $k-1$ terms from a divergent series results in a divergent series.\n\nMore precisely, assume ${a}_{n}$ is well-defined for $n\\ge 1$ and $k\\ge 1$ is an integer. Then, we have the following:\n\n*If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also divergent.*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257613 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257614 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257615 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257616 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257617 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257618 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257619 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257620 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257620 13194139533864 true] [17592186257612 1110 #uuid "d2d0d90d-66d3-54f5-a712-29e05a119d40" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257613 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257613 1111 #uuid "23e27595-0a81-5428-9abb-089c83c08a05" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257614 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257614 1111 #uuid "9345163d-02cc-5438-87af-72f9c7ee5893" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257615 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257615 1111 #uuid "1c66f9e1-7093-5248-babb-26644ce91839" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257616 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257616 1111 #uuid "3f944afb-cc01-513f-8688-1027dbd1a9e3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257617 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257617 1111 #uuid "b7ce0565-dbc7-52a4-b169-d172edd975cc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257618 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257618 1111 #uuid "33220375-c9f2-51c0-b090-41092480c806" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257619 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257619 1111 #uuid "442a40ce-f652-5e35-8b50-d1e22420cb13" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257620 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257620 1111 #uuid "4ec4cb49-cedd-56c8-9b45-dc0e15e2bbd1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257622 13194139533864 true] [17592186257621 1089 "q-124086" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257621 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - $-{10}^{500}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent\nII. - ${\\sum }_{n=25}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}-{10}^{500}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257621 1113 #uuid "b0132ee2-97f1-5701-b78e-440561d08c8c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257621 1145 "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is false. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is false. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257623 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257624 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257625 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257626 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257627 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257628 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257629 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257630 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257626 13194139533864 true] [17592186257622 1110 #uuid "907ac348-0d31-53aa-a507-4f3224e0eb36" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257623 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257623 1111 #uuid "93784fbc-83fc-552e-bca4-b879f0cba48b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257624 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257624 1111 #uuid "39dc14bc-8f7b-5dc0-8c25-db4ce0daa200" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257625 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257625 1111 #uuid "e8f6245f-990b-5cb6-ac0d-2f2ad6dedd8c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257626 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257626 1111 #uuid "58f239de-e4fd-55ef-a60a-235d023bd6dc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257627 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257627 1111 #uuid "513ed02a-8b72-53e8-ab93-d7cda8f774bc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257628 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257628 1111 #uuid "eb95d64c-4c75-5942-9e5f-6610b98a0140" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257629 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257629 1111 #uuid "5f45a70f-c513-545e-9bae-0dea0270c330" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257630 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257630 1111 #uuid "11df1ff9-b048-5c6b-afa7-e4921a4772e3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257632 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1089 "q-124087" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=100}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent\nII. - $-{10}^{10}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=100}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}-{10}^{10}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1113 #uuid "a5033c15-e0ed-52f4-b026-2ec54fd36d33" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1145 "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is true. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257633 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257634 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257635 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257636 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257637 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257638 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257639 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257640 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257633 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1110 #uuid "6bf54287-4698-5a94-9cac-64d208e87386" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257633 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257633 1111 #uuid "6940f8b5-519f-52c4-bcac-f863b7c3b82e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1103 #