c{1}{{n}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis is a $p$-series with $p=3.$ Since $p>1,$ the series is convergent.\n\nNote that the factor of $\\frac{5}{2}$ multiplying the series has no effect on the convergence/divergence of the series." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257765 13194139533864 true] [17592186257764 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257764 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257764 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257765 13194139533864 true] [17592186257764 1110 #uuid "db64e579-2ebf-5f08-88cd-da538103aeb4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257765 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257765 1111 #uuid "d133462b-1549-5105-a881-96650fbe79ea" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257766 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257767 13194139533864 true] [17592186257766 1089 "q-125257" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257766 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257766 1100 "Which of the following series are convergent?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{n\\sqrt[3]{{n}^{2}}}$\nII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3{n}^{4}}$\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5\\sqrt[3]{n}}{\\sqrt{n}}$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257766 1113 #uuid "79f1c9d5-2149-5539-a2fe-8aa88505e603" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257766 1145 "We analyze each series in turn.\n\n- First, we look at ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{n\\sqrt[3]{{n}^{2}}}.$ Rewriting this series gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{n\\sqrt[3]{{n}^{2}}} & =2{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n\\cdot {n}^{2/3}} \\\\  & =2{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{5/3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand this is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{5}{3}.$ Since $p>1,$ the series converges by the $p$-series test.\n\n- For the second series, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3{n}^{4}}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{4}}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=4.$ Since $p>1,$ the series is convergent.\n\n- For the third series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5\\sqrt[3]{n}}{\\sqrt{n}} & =5{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{1/3}}{{n}^{1/2}} \\\\  & =5{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{1/6}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand this is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{1}{6}.$ Since $p\\le 1,$ the series diverges by the $p$-series test.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257768 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257769 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257770 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257771 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257772 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257773 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257774 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257775 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257773 13194139533864 true] [17592186257767 1110 #uuid "d57bfeb9-ff6f-5f21-8379-8a644a1e8993" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257768 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257768 1111 #uuid "3912c428-8308-54b9-90a5-343e36b58e8d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257769 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257769 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257769 1111 #uuid "a229ba77-fdb2-518d-85ef-4ca70a20e0c2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257770 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257770 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257770 1111 #uuid "9c355002-1b19-50ea-85dc-9abb1f0d9285" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257771 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257771 1103 #