fty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}$ is also divergent for $K\\ne 0.$\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also divergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Any non-zero multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is true. The sum of a convergent series and a divergent series is divergent.\n\n- Statement III is true. Note that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{50}{b}_{n}$ is a **finite series.** Therefore, ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{50}{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258499 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258500 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258501 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258502 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258503 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258504 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258505 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258506 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258499 13194139533864 true] [17592186258498 1110 #uuid "4ad3a4e2-a944-5a9b-86c6-00785b7a28c4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258499 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186258499 1111 #uuid "22494098-8b65-5fa2-b2be-110fdcb3be8e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258500 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17