258507 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $a=\\frac{1}{4},$ $b=3,$ and $c=5.$ So, we calculate the discriminant as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =(3)^{2}-4(\\frac{1}{4})(5) \\\\  & =9-5 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd $4={2}^{2}$ is a perfect square.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFirst, notice that our quadratic equation has rational coefficients. And, since the discriminant is a nonzero perfect square, the equation must have two rational solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258509 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258510 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258511 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258512 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258513 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258514 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258515 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258516 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258514 13194139533864 true] [17592186258508 1110 #uuid "74b083b9-77c7-56f1-b51c-d9c941c7b67b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258509 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258509 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186258509 1111 #uuid "a5e19740-66b8-5f96-9e7c-a955bd088956" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258510 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258510 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186258510 1111 #uuid "9246247b-5d70-5428-b3ec-20f913e45a67" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258511 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258511 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [175921862585