3$ | $-8$ | $-15$ | $-24$ | $-35$ |" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259612 13194139533864 true] [17592186259611 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259611 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259611 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259612 13194139533864 true] [17592186259611 1110 #uuid "56edae5f-cb40-59c1-ab3c-e3780d816bb3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259612 1034 "7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259612 1111 #uuid "2444c709-d123-5806-a9dd-efcb4142d7c2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259614 13194139533864 true] [17592186259613 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259613 1041 "field-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259613 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259614 13194139533864 true] [17592186259613 1110 #uuid "dfb086a3-c35b-5665-aba1-7223cff63bb6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259614 1034 "213" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259614 1111 #uuid "f9a2a163-0346-5e9c-9fe0-f4cad81b99e5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259616 13194139533864 true] [17592186259615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259615 1041 "field-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259616 13194139533864 true] [17592186259615 1110 #uuid "c4eaa414-d93f-5dbe-9d15-6c71f8462269" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259616 1034 "-8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259616 1111 #uuid "0a7835fe-8c51-5047-bad9-73b70954bbe8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259617 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259618 13194139533864 true] [17592186259617 1089 "q-32634" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259617 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259617 1100 "If $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}(4x)+5,$ find ${({f}^{-1})}^{'}(x)$ as a function of ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259617 1113 #uuid "506e531d-5777-544e-ae01-6ba51aecd58b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259617 1145 "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\operatorname{cos}(4x)+5,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}(4y)+5\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{cos}(4y)+5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}(4y)\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =-4\\operatorname{sin}(4y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{sin}(4y)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}(4y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}(4{f}^{-1}(x)) \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{'}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}(4{f}^{-1}(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259619 13194139533864 true] [17592186259618 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259618 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259618 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259619 13194139533864 true] [17592186259618 1110 #uuid "bd27c77e-9e5d-5327-80f6-9f1ae988bd0c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259619 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}(4{f}^{-1}(x))" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259619 1111 #uuid "bd8f67de-5aae-59a6-ade5-f44783342ea6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259620 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259621 13194139533864 true] [17592186259620 1089 "q-32640" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259620 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259620 1100 "If $h(x)=\\sqrt{5x-1},$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{'}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259620 1113 #uuid "8c4b70c3-5b64-5323-b3fa-be629ae754ba" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259620 1145 "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\sqrt{5x-1},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5y-1}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{5y-1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}((5y-1)^{1/2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{1}{2}(5y-1)^{-1/2}\\cdot 5 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5y-1}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5y-1}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5{h}^{-1}(x)-1}}{5} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5{h}^{-1}(x)-1}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259622 13194139533864 true] [17592186259621 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259621 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259621 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259622 13194139533864 true] [17592186259621 1110 #uuid "87509928-4c83-533c-88a1-c2eea0388b62" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259622 1034 "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5{h}^{-1}(x)-1}}{5}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259622 1111 #uuid "83f64d46-9f19-54a3-ac8e-a7cd4956bbc2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259623 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259624 13194139533864 true] [17592186259623 1089 "q-32667" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259623 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259623 1100 "If $x=2{y}^{2}+7y-\\frac{3}{y},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259623 1113 #uuid "38d85cd9-88e6-5905-afcb-0031bdcaa356" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259623 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+7y-\\frac{3}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+7y-3{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4y+7+3{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =4y+7+\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{3}+7{y}^{2}+3}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4{y}^{3}+7{y}^{2}+3}.\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259624 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259625 13194139533864 true] [17592186259624 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259624 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259624 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259625 13194139533864 true] [17592186259624 1110 #uuid "d3f51f12-e451-594f-869b-72bd15f5744f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259625 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4{y}^{3}+7{y}^{2}+3}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259625 1111 #uuid "75130659-30f6-5366-b3db-366c72707f68" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259626 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259627 13194139533864 true] [17592186259626 1089 "q-32711" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259626 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259626 1100 "Given a curve $x=6{y}^{2}+2y-5,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(3,1)?$\n\n$y =$: {{y}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259626 1113 #uuid "8c5a53a4-5df1-54f4-9072-6706e9600229" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259626 1145 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(6{y}^{2}+2y-5) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (2y)+2(1)+0 \\\\  & =12y+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{12y+2}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(3,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12\\cdot 1+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{14}(x-3) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{14}-\\frac{3}{14}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{14}+\\frac{11}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259627 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259628 13194139533864 true] [17592186259627 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259627 1041 "y" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259627 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259628 13194139533864 true] [17592186259627 1110 #uuid "9e700a7c-3d97-5125-9a0d-686655d7ccc7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259628 1034 "\\frac{x+11}{14}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259628 1111 #uuid "2c69f652-d683-57cf-8b43-c7ed8131d2b2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259630 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259632 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259634 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1089 "q-327473" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/0279244ec15b12209fa0a18b46bb9a52622878221c9d424b082f73feefae109d.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $-(x-4)(x+1)<0.$\n\nThe solution to the inequality is \n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\nor $x>$\n{{field-3}}." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1113 #uuid "d4e62bc6-3f98-510b-80a4-0b7f3a3e5668" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259629 1145 "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x-4)(x+1)<0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny=-(x-4)(x+1)\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/3153ee62691b0000cbf249553c93a7304c3a2908d2ea7810874c5ed37e68a412.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-1$ or $x>4.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259631 13194139533864 true] [17592186259630 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259630 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259630 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259631 13194139533864 true] [17592186259630 1110 #uuid "8337e4b4-8dc2-5dac-b1a4-957add5cd55d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259631 1034 "<" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259631 1111 #uuid "f0e18a3e-e437-5238-81ec-648bc6251417" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259633 13194139533864 true] [17592186259632 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259632 1041 "field-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259632 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259633 13194139533864 true] [1759218