ort-ready/assets/373430993d1b1d46a92b44ed897c5e4570b6a9c9072e5b9a4af2b854b7801c81.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-1<x<5.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259638 13194139533864 true] [17592186259637 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259637 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259637 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259638 13194139533864 true] [17592186259637 1110 #uuid "7da33b69-14fe-594b-8b1b-b35ccf76db47" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259638 1034 "-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259638 1111 #uuid "3288736e-6f5c-50d6-8b7b-ebc88d608e1c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259640 13194139533864 true] [17592186259639 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259639 1041 "field-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259639 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259640 13194139533864 true] [17592186259639 1110 #uuid "f9b8e9a1-90e8-5cbf-aa55-0193e94c694a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259640 1034 "<" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259640 1111 #uuid "94d3b5f0-2cb7-51f8-bc28-ee01d1025e47" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259641 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259642 13194139533864 true] [17592186259641 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259641 1041 "field-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259641 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259642 13194139533864 true] [17592186259641 1110 #uuid "d0af7488-dde8-5f4d-85b7-2b6201e188bd" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259642 1034 "5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259642 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259642 1111 #uuid "f7baffe6-f715-53fb-ba6e-3e5bd328657a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259644 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259646 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259648 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259650 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259652 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259654 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1089 "q-327882" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1100 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}\\theta -3,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sin}\\theta +1,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}}\n$\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}{{field-5}}\n$y\\le $\n{{field-6}}." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1113 #uuid "d112c55a-dce1-5cd1-8ca7-5af9f3e1be71" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259643 1145 "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -5 & \\le 5\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 5 \\\\ -5-3 & \\le 5\\operatorname{cos}\\theta -3\\le 5-3 \\\\ -8 & \\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-8\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -7 & \\le 7\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le 7 \\\\ -7+1 & \\le 7\\operatorname{sin}\\theta +1\\le 7+1 \\\\ -6 & \\le y\\le 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-6\\le y\\le 8.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259645 13194139533864 true] [17592186259644 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259644 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259644 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259645 13194139533864 true] [17592186259644 1110 #uuid "3d9b9049-f21c-58f9-9b9c-7729345a0b9a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259645 1034 "-8" 1