17592186259653 13194139533864 true] [17592186259652 1110 #uuid "19c90fad-d16f-50d9-9185-838ddae679eb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259653 1034 "\\le " 13194139533864 true] [17592186259653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259653 1111 #uuid "e9d2a8ca-d701-51d7-9978-85ecb38c295c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259655 13194139533864 true] [17592186259654 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259654 1041 "field-6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259654 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259655 13194139533864 true] [17592186259654 1110 #uuid "c911e62e-1ba4-593b-bbb3-d311554d083d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259655 1034 "8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259655 1111 #uuid "75189aac-a3eb-5fb3-8990-84a8a573c84d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259656 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259657 13194139533864 true] [17592186259656 1089 "q-328242" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259656 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259656 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,\\frac{1}{3}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259656 1113 #uuid "47d2cbf1-1164-5cb5-ab6c-facf3e8732c7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259656 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =\\pi +2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ 6x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=\\frac{1}{9}.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259658 13194139533864 true] [17592186259657 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259657 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259657 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259658 13194139533864 true] [17592186259657 1110 #uuid "5c059408-4e1e-56d3-9bee-5e0446a61f1a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259658 1034 "\\frac{1}{9}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259658 1111 #uuid "8481b97c-79bd-5680-a936-855eee350617" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259660 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259662 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259664 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259666 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1089 "q-328346" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}(2x+{45}^{∘})=1,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1113 #uuid "2ef87672-04a1-57b6-b8ef-a21f1ff660eb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259659 1145 "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-{45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={0}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={90}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={180}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={270}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={0}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={90}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={270}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259661 13194139533864 true] [17592186259660 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259660 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259660 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259661 13194139533864 true] [17592186259660 1110 #uuid "6313b72d-4ece-5327-8d7f-7d8b27de6a3b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259661 1034 "0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259661 1111 #uuid "6c158c77-0adb-5f06-8d4b-c07d37822cc7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259663 13194139533864 true] [17592186259662 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259662 1041 "field-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259662 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259663 13194139533864 true] [17592186259662 1110 #uuid "ee14a56f-6429-5c5e-a654-22356ab98625" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259663 1034 "90" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259663 1111 #uuid "2f7935d6-915d-546d-9ca6-05f8521d9bd0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259665 13194139533864 true] [17592186259664 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259664 1041 "field-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259664 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259665 13194139533864 true] [17592186259664 1110 #uuid "79538ab1-c604-5e0b-ab5a-c1801bb24957" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259665 1034 "180" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259665 1111 #uuid "797a29ae-b1ec-5db8-ac8e-934955f9ac1f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259666 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259667 13194139533864 true] [17592186259666 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 