ke the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3\\operatorname{tan}(2y-1)) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =3{sec}^{2}(2y-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =6{sec}^{2}(2y-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{6{sec}^{2}(2y-1)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}(2y-1)}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}(2{f}^{-1}(x)-1)}{6} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}(2{f}^{-1}(x)-1)}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259691 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259692 13194139533864 true] [17592186259691 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259691 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259691 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259692 13194139533864 true] [17592186259691 1110 #uuid "2ce2b902-e5bf-5ba7-a987-8f030fd802fa" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259692 1034 "\\frac{{cos}^{2}(2{f}^{-1}(x)-1)}{6}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259692 1111 #uuid "b8ca8cc8-40fb-5b61-956e-ab3c8ddf2f4b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259693 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259694 13194139533864 true] [17592186259693 1089 "q-332158" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259693 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259693 1100 "Using the fact that ${75}^{∘}={45}^{∘}+{30}^{∘},$\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘}).$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}({75}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259693 1113 #uuid "cbd2c5fc-c58b-57db-ac30-a7a42b7e4318" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259693 1145 "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}(x+y)=\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}y+\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}y\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $x={45}^{∘}$ an