60b2018-b639-5013-ac54-7fe6b71f58fe" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259863 1034 "-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259863 1111 #uuid "46387cb9-77c6-5309-9165-30b1b22f3401" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259864 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259865 13194139533864 true] [17592186259864 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259864 1041 "field-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259864 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259865 13194139533864 true] [17592186259864 1110 #uuid "00e11637-23e5-564b-a2cf-551237109653" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259865 1034 "2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259865 1111 #uuid "3eb759e9-9584-5702-9892-b88d8e48dfa7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259866 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259867 13194139533864 true] [17592186259866 1089 "q-339973" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259866 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186259866 1100 "Given that $y=2\\operatorname{ln}x+{x}^{\\pi }+1$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259866 1113 #uuid "56a1c713-cc3d-50c8-8cb6-4fdd7363b496" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259866 1145 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}x+{x}^{\\pi }+1) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{x})+\\pi {x}^{\\pi -1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\pi {x}^{\\pi -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259867 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259868 13194139533864 true] [17592186259867 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259867 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259867 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259868 13194139533864 true] [17592186259867 1110 #uuid "34024961-12fc-58f9-a76e-e8aa412781dd" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259868 1034 "\\frac{2}{x}+\\pi {x}^{\\pi -1}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259868 1111 #uuid "dbff73c0-4107-5d2d-80ee-2e309969accb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259869 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259870 13194139533864 true] [17592186259869 1089 "q-339989" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259869 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259869 1100 "Given the function $y=4{x}^{2}-6{log}_{3}x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259869 1113 #uuid "8da817ac-8d36-5248-8a56-e3e3305933b1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259869 1145 "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2}-6{log}_{3}x) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2x-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =8x-\\frac{6}{x\\operatorname{ln}3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(8x-\\frac{6}{x\\operatorname{ln}3})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =8(1)-\\frac{6}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259871 13194139533864 true] [17592186259870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259870 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259871 13194139533864 true] [17592186259870 1110 #uuid "ee0c8a1e-b0e6-5071-94f7-653e925f1fa1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259871 1034 "8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259871 1111 #uuid "4b574247-6baf-54d0-8f4a-cab77cc1c36c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259872 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259873 13194139533864 true] [17592186259872 1089 "q-339997" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259872 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259872 1100 "Given that $f(x)={log}_{7}x-3\\operatorname{ln}x$, find ${f}^{'}(x).$\n\n${f}^{'}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259872 1113 #uuid "1b0635f8-e7ae-5a1b-959e-70b659ecfb4d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259872 1145 "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{7}x-3\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{7}x)-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-3(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259873 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259874 13194139533864 true] [17592186259873 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259873 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259873 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259874 13194139533864 true] [17592186259873 1110 #uuid "49b73348-7610-5233-9840-8f3bef55321f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259874 1034 "\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259874 1111 #uuid "3ab0884e-e31a-5ed4-a2b3-d2fad90cbba3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259875 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259876 13194139533864 true] [17592186259875 1089 "q-340014" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259875 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259875 1100 "Given the function $y=5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259875 1113 #uuid "84b41208-fbbb-5c93-b4f6-118635b12b3e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259875 1145 "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2x+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =10x+\\frac{6}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(10x+\\frac{6}{x})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 3+\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =32\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259876 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259877 13194139533864 true] [17592186259876 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259876 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259876 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259877 13194139533864 true] [17592186259876 1110 #uuid "9364ab94-e028-59cc-bb87-1b9ee5e2b212" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259877 1034 "32" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259877 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259877 1111 #uuid "bdd5f721-f706-5012-82b2-dd84492aa8b4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259878 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259879 13194139533864 true] [17592186259878 1089 "q-340022" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259878 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259878 1100 "Given the function $y=5\\operatorname{ln}x-2\\cdot {3}^{x},$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259878 1113 #uuid "c733d8c4-483f-51cd-af63-0208432f9f16" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259878 1145 "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{ln}x-2\\cdot {3}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}-2\\cdot {3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}3 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{5}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{x})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259880 13194139533864 true] [17592186259879 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259879 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259879 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259880 13194139533864 true] [17592186259879 1110 #uuid "93c1c169-e1a5-562c-9421-a536a3e6f150" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259880 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259880 1111 #uuid "7efa9c47-eb42-5217-9b01-9324dffcf05f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259881 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259882 13194139533864 true] [17592186259881 1089 "q-340087" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259881 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259881 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}{log}_{4}(9x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259881 1113 #uuid "c4b20c1c-6829-532a-8642-48abc149b75a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259881 1145 "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{4}(9x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/1ead64d0b64a005122fa34c65677d5e7980c2a76245bbaca572325b8681ae958.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\le 0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}{log}_{4}(9x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x>0.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}{log}_{4}(9x)=-\\infty .\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259883 13194139533864 true] [17592186259882 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259882 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259882 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259883 13194139533864 true] [17592186259882 1110 #uuid "4e77ef3b-fe07-5d48-950d-dd2eb6ff6cfb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259883 1034 "-\\infty " 13194139533864 true] [17592186259883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259883 1111 #uuid "7f7824ed-d5d8-5046-89e2-611be36b1699" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259884 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259885 13194139533864 true] [17592186259884 1089 "q-340109" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259884 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259884 1100 "Given the function $y=-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259884 1113 #uuid "2238b6dc-d73b-58d3-b7fe-799bc2a1f221" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259884 1145 "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{2}{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259886 13194139533864 true] [17592186259885 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259885 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259885 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259886 13194139533864 true] [17592186259885 1110 #uuid "e6bbf671-b44c-59c0-9d96-625daffa19cb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259886 1034 "-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259886 1111 #uuid "ecadcc24-e607-5843-a6b4-9068f95f75d2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259887 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259888 13194139533864 true] [17592186259887 1089 "q-340290" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259887 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259887 1100 "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}$, find ${f}^{'}(x).$\n\n${f}^{'}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259887 1113 #uuid "94125d6a-8fad-58e8-9ce8-c6017b8b43a0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259887 1145 "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=2$ and $v(x)={x}^{2},$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{'}(x) & =0, \\\\ {v}^{'}(x) & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x}{{({x}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4x}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259888 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259889 13194139533864 true] [17592186259888 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259888 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259888 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259889 13194139533864 true] [17592186259888 1110 #uuid "263f54f4-c409-5d72-ae68-c6f60c986993" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259889 1034 "-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259889 1111 #uuid "e4931bc9-bc91-5131-a954-bdb1771462eb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259890 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259891 13194139533864 true] [17592186259890 1089 "q-340307" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259890 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259890 1100 "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}c-x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-1\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=2.$ What is the value of the constant $c?$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259890 1113 #uuid "7ddd0688-dbb1-5edb-8d08-525b26a06be7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259890 1145 "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)$ to be equal to $8,$ the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal to $2.$\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x<-1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=c-x.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}c-x \\\\  & =c-(-1) \\\\  & =c+1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>-1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x-1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}{x}^{2}-2x-1 \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-2(-1)-1 \\\\  & =1+2-1 \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) \\\\ c+1 & =2 \\\\ c & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259892 13194139533864 true] [17592186259891 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259891 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259891 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259892 13194139533864 true] [17592186259891 1110 #uuid "7fec6cb4-e826-5dbe-bb32-219c987b8a6f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259892 1034 "1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259892 1111 #uuid "7528b06a-a2d6-5ebb-bfb3-2d4a4bd9e29b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259893 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259894 13194139533864 true] [17592186259893 1089 "q-340318" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259893 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259893 1100 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{x}{{e}^{3x}},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=1.$\n\nThe slope at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259893 1113 #uuid "876d6c3c-d8bf-5b17-84ad-fecbaeadd41d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259893 1145 "In this case, the expression for $y$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)={e}^{3x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(x)}^{'}\\cdot {e}^{3x}-x\\cdot {({e}^{3x})}^{'}}{{({e}^{3x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{3x}-x\\cdot 3{e}^{3x}}{{({e}^{3x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}(1-3x)}{{({e}^{3x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-3x}{{e}^{3x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=1$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}\\,(1) & =\\frac{1-3(1)}{{e}^{3(1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{e}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at $x=1$ is $-\\frac{2}{{e}^{3}}.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259895 13194139533864 true] [17592186259894 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259894 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259894 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259895 13194139533864 true] [17592186259894 1110 #uuid "c5516765-62a1-566d-a1a7-d1e93e58037d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259895 1034 "-\\frac{2}{{e}^{3}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259895 1111 #uuid "9b4bc067-52c1-585d-8b3e-e01f0fb731fe" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259896 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259897 13194139533864 true] [17592186259896 1089 "q-340336" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259896 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259896 1100 "Given that $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}x}{{x}^{2}}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}\n$).$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259896 1113 #uuid "b4792b81-53a1-5620-92e3-e7ad1403e4ee" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259896 1145 "Let $u=\\operatorname{tan}x$ and $v={x}^{2}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}x\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\cdot {sec}^{2}x-\\operatorname{tan}x\\cdot 2x}{{({x}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(x{sec}^{2}x-2\\operatorname{tan}x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\,x{sec}^{2}x-2\\operatorname{tan}x\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259897 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259898 13194139533864 true] [17592186259897 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259897 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259897 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259898 13194139533864 true] [17592186259897 1110 #uuid "acd4aa7d-7e27-5239-b341-720c28271e92" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259898 1034 "x{sec}^{2}x-2\\operatorname{tan}x" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259898 1111 #uuid "43f21534-dc51-584d-bce2-28232b621df8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259899 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259900 13194139533864 true] [17592186259899 1089 "q-340340" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259899 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259899 1100 "Given that $y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x+1},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259899 1113 #uuid "5ffdc549-0c35-5d99-abd9-dd981b4eb66f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259899 1145 "Let $u={e}^{x}$ and $v=x+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)\\cdot {e}^{x}-{e}^{x}\\cdot 1}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(x+1-1)}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{x}}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259901 13194139533864 true] [17592186259900 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259900 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259900 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259901 13194139533864 true] [17592186259900 1110 #uuid "efa6c8ef-b590-53a3-958a-ec1a9341ec79" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259901 1034 "\\frac{x{e}^{x}}{(x+1)^{2}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259901 1111 #uuid "4a0b4d1e-797e-5ae7-9daa-2d05442e5018" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259902 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259903 13194139533864 true] [17592186259902 1089 "q-340642" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259902 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259902 1100 "Find the slope $m$ of $y=g(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ if $g(x)=\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259902 1113 #uuid "0c556fe2-0de3-5c83-a8df-8864a240ec1e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259902 1145 "First, we calculate the derivative using the product rule and sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{csc}x\\operatorname{cot}x)(\\operatorname{cot}x)+(\\operatorname{csc}x)(-{csc}^{2}x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}x({cot}^{2}x+{csc}^{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and evaluate the slope $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={g}^{'}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\operatorname{csc}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})[{cot}^{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{csc}^{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =-1\\cdot ({0}^{2}+{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259903 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259904 13194139533864 true] [17592186259903 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259903 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259903 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259904 13194139533864 true] [17592186259903 1110 #uuid "fcc7f983-afa9-534d-9d90-007ddaf612bf" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259904 1034 "-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259904 1111 #uuid "73911311-b113-5748-be58-21901c884257" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259905 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259906 13194139533864 true] [17592186259905 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259908 13194139533864 true] [17592186259905 1089 "q-340942" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259905 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259905 1100 "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=2{x}^{2}+1$ at the point $(2,9).$\n\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259905 1113 #uuid "f1ee8101-ef90-5936-9218-2b307b36327b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259905 1145 "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+1.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n{f}^{'}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+1)=4x\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,9):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{'}(2)=4(2)=8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{'}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-9 & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x-2) \\\\ 8y-72 & =-x+2 \\\\ x+8\\cdot y & =74.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259907 13194139533864 true] [17592186259906 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259906 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259906 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259907 13194139533864 true] [175921862599