[17592186261248 1100 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x?$\n\nI. - $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\nII. - $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\nIII. - $(\\sqrt{3},-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261248 1113 #uuid "b051727c-2d33-5ba7-828f-c75227488b69" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261248 1145 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\sqrt{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261250 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261251 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261252 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261253 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261254 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261255 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261256 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261257 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1104 #edb/ref 17592186261253 13194139533864 true] [17592186261249 1110 #uuid "d3cff461-a7c4-5449-83d4-576218bc4146" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261250 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261250 1111 #uuid "c3df2432-d0b3-55da-bb5f-06253adf8bae" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261251 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261251 1111 #uuid "7712557a-7be5-5f7f-9c67-4d99cd9aa572" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261252 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261252 1111 #uuid "eedd3e10-4981-51c4-9dd9-db253d883611" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261253 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261253 1111 #uuid "627a980f-c83e-5930-8f39-3e3aa302d02b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261254 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261254 1111 #uuid "f930a2ff-2e31-57a7-94aa-f1776ffcdd83" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261255 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261255 1111 #uuid "c29eba9f-8b94-583e-aa05-3b9512acc2ff" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261256 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261256 1111 #uuid "0fea163c-b666-5d70-960e-245dd1e65817" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261257 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261257 1111 #uuid "619e2a91-10dd-555f-9125-519e91fc7680" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261258 1017 #edb/ref 17592186261259 13194139533864 true] [17592186261258 1089 "q-70881" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261258 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186261258 1100 "Given that $y=2\\operatorname{ln}x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261258 1113 #uuid "ddbc5046-3110-56db-8516-2c66301e420e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261258 1145 "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261260 13194139533864 true] [17592186261259 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186261259 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261259 1104 #edb/ref 17592186261260 13194139533864 true] [17592186261259 1110 #uuid "a4834572-d0d9-5af8-9ee4-eb52c2ba9fba" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261260 1034 "\\frac{2}{x}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186261260 1111 #uuid "b522e060-fe6b-5463-838f-6312307330aa" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261261 1017 #edb/ref 17592186261262 13194139533864 true] [17592186261261 1089 "q-70897" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261261 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186261261 1100 "Given that $y=2{log}_{2}x+{2}^{x}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=2.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261261 1113 #uuid "9194b183-89a8-5cf0-9567-8d024e74d060" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261261 1145 "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}2\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}2)|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+4\\operatorname{ln}2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261263 13194139533864 true] [17592186261262 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186261262 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261262 1104 #edb/ref 17592186261263 13194139533864 true] [17592186261262 1110 #uuid "d6a7b0e3-b7de-5a49-bb4f-9f16b34e5de5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261263 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+4\\operatorname{ln}2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186261263 1111 #uuid "53fa7533-ef15-5cdb-886b-85d4552daab9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261264 1017 #edb/ref 17592186261265 13194139533864 true] [17592186261264 1089 "q-70907" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261264 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186261264 1100 "Which of the following equations have no real solution?\n\nI. - $\\sqrt{3x+1}=-1$\nII. - $-\\sqrt{4-x}=6$\nIII. - $\\sqrt{2x+1}=1$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261264 1113 #uuid "fd9d77ea-492f-56f5-8abf-5300e4f7832a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261264 1145 "Remember that a square root is always positive or zero. So, a radical equation has no real solution if it states that a square root is equal to a negative number.\n\nOf the given equations, only I and II state that a square root is equal to a negative number. Therefore, equations I and II have no real solution.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261266 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261267 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261268 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261269 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261270 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261271 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261272 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1000 #edb/ref 17592186261273 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1104 #edb/ref 17592186261271 13194139533864 true] [17592186261265 1110 #uuid "db82101f-7c0e-501d-90c5-0ffe2bb275d8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261266 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261266 1111 #uuid "99746b9a-db42-5c76-8f6b-77a4de7baadd" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261267 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261267 1111 #uuid "7eb5cd38-555a-5de4-ad48-126e9197b058" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261268 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186261268 1111 #uuid "c143786c-c752-5d2e-9903-0c52b74f138f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261269 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186261269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [175