"q-9337" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262007 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186262007 1100 "Determine whether the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{{n}^{4}}}$\nconverges or diverges.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262007 1113 #uuid "b19142ea-49a5-5749-b0b5-ee3907a47a2f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262007 1145 "The series can be written as\n\n$$\n2{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{4/3}},\n$$\n\nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{4}{3}.$ Since $p>1$, the series is convergent. \n\nNote that the factor of $2$ multiplying the series has no effect on the convergence/divergence \nof the series." 13194139533864 true] [17592186262008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262009 13194139533864 true] [17592186262008 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186262008 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262008 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262009 13194139533864 true] [17592186262008 1110 #uuid "df143856-fb55-5527-a503-a0ef018edd46" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262009 1034 "2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186262009 1111 #uuid "a5a9a0ac-ec3f-5328-b510-e2373b85173e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262010 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262011 13194139533864 true] [17592186262010 1089 "q-956" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262010 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186262010 1100 "Calculate ${log}_{8}(32)$ without using a calculator.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262010 1113 #uuid "04859e81-899a-55b9-b72c-cdf329ab2df5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262010 1145 "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}X=\\frac{{log}_{b}X}{{log}_{b}a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8,$ and $X=32.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $2,$ we set $b=2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}(32) & =\\frac{{log}_{2}(32)}{{log}_{2}(8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}({2}^{5})}{{log}_{2}({2}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262011 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262012 13194139533864 true] [17592186262011 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186262011 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262011 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262012 13194139533864 true] [17592186262011 1110 #uuid "52b95d39-7d74-5974-8d4e-39079c7d9ed6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262012 1034 "\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186262012 1111 #uuid "27b0bc67-9e69-591a-af43-9f9d6f672b43" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262013 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262014 13194139533864 true] [17592186262013 1089 "q-96669" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186262013 1100 "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nI. - ${y}^{‴}+(\\operatorname{sin}x){y}^{'}={x}^{2}y$\nII. - $5{y}^{''}{y}^{'}+3xy=4{y}^{'}$\nIII. - ${({y}^{'})}^{2}-2{x}^{2}=y$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262013 1113 #uuid "e356353f-6fc7-5ad8-bdec-cdea5919a2a0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262013 1145 "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation II is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262015 13194139533864 true] [17592186262014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262016 13194139533864 true] [17592186262014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262017 13194139533864 true] [17592186262014