fferential equation. We see that it is of the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ where $f(y)=\\operatorname{ln}y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262055 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262056 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262057 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262058 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262059 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262060 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262061 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262062 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262056 13194139533864 true] [17592186262054 1110 #uuid "75ce830f-f7ad-5a8f-80c9-bfdeca211ffb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262055 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262055 1111 #uuid "260ab397-b927-5671-a132-7dd09d609d34" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262056 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262056 1111 #uuid "7f06ae2a-7201-5a3b-99b4-8509ecf16acd" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262057 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262057 1111 #uuid "8077e54d-7a37-5429-8fa9-ae9e74524229" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262058 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262058 1111 #uuid "0dd93856-caf5-588c-b235-bc48388d2a25" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262059 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262059 1111 #uuid "22e76f62-d0c3-5a80-bbc8-c2dc099d27b2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262060 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262060 1111 #uuid "6aa4a613-9929-59a9-ba2b-6961e9f0f413" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262061 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262061 1111 #uuid "51c281f4-b71a-50f5-b47b-39e1bf734f00" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262062 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262062 1111 #uuid "65c7d200-aec2-5a6c-8d68-07f6d3c47302" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262063 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262064 13194139533864 true] [17592186262063 1089 "q-96705" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262063 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186262063 1100 "Which of the following are autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nI. - ${e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3}=0$\nII. - $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x=\\operatorname{ln}y$\nIII. - $5x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x}=0$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262063 1113 #uuid "2f8c44a4-8695-5bce-9b85-93159ef8f779" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262063 1145 "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation I is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{3}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=3{y}^{3}{e}^{-y}.$\n\n- Equation II is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x & =\\operatorname{ln}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{ln}y+2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}y+2x.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation III is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{5{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{5{x}^{2}}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262065 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262066 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262067 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262068 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262069 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262070 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262071 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262072 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262068 13194139533864 true] [17592186262064 1110 #uuid "b143ce9c-1d2f-54f8-9822-2eb13785f2e4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262065 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262065 1111 #uuid "b74d4121-19bd-519b-9f42-6e2d74a4e53e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262066 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262066 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262066 1111 #uuid "974d493e-45f3-5112-9946-af67f80df4aa" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262067 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262067 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262067 1111 #uuid "aae8832f-c0df-5015-9905-eda5a0e98849" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262068 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262068 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262068 1111 #uuid "8784430a-fefb-5a0e-8037-7072e097a072" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262069 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262069 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262069 1111 #uuid "e76fcc33-5ba1-50a2-b5ef-7bdb0d465af6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262070 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262070 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262070 1111 #uuid "59f18cbc-4413-5cee-a2a2-0a7277b9cd1c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262071 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262071 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262071 1111 #uuid "710af5b4-256e-512a-a5d1-86c2b6361f9a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262072 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262072 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262072 1111 #uuid "b70c79e3-f5b6-5da6-92fe-75d7cf1ec1e5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262073 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262074 13194139533864 true] [17592186262073 1089 "q-96712" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262073 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186262073 1100 "Which of the following are **not** autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nI. - ${y}^{'}=1-\\sqrt{y}$\nII. - ${y}^{'}-\\operatorname{tan}y={e}^{2}$\nIII. - $x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y}=4$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262073 1113 #uuid "a6f5f12c-8742-57e1-8431-b7e5f7c8b33f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262073 1145 "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation I is an autonomous differential equation. It is of the form ${y}^{'}=f(y),$ where $f(y)=1-\\sqrt{y}.$\n\n- Equation II is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form ${y}^{'}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{'}-\\operatorname{tan}y & ={e}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =\\operatorname{tan}y+{e}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\operatorname{tan}y+{e}^{2}.$\n\n- Equation III is *not* an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y} & =4 \\\\ {y}^{'} & =\\frac{4y+1}{xy} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{4y+1}{xy}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262075 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262076 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262077 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262078 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262079 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262080 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262081 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262082 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262079 13194139533864 true] [17592186262074 1110 #uuid "831ff5c2-b840-5fe4-b6ea-ec995d5e6729" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262075 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262075 1111 #uuid "60ed9cbb-4ba4-51aa-a0f8-7225e1688c36" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262076 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262076 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262076 1111 #uuid "31036b5b-7449-5599-8b7f-8b39b778f239" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262077 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262077 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262077 1111 #uuid "be9955de-2d2b-52bd-ad19-a9c11284301d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262078 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262078 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262078 1111 #uuid "c053f2d6-9364-55b3-954f-91552728a08d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262079 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262079 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262079 1111 #uuid "8163967d-e6d8-56ce-9dca-756d234c3020" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262080 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262080 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262080 1111 #uuid "11bda8cf-ada4-544f-8e86-30b984916eaa" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262081 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262081 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262081 1111 #uuid "f1a652c4-ff96-5e6d-b026-86d6eed744a5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262082 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262082 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186262082 1111 #uuid "9e078445-c2fc-5a31-88ab-c2be941bd0f4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262083 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262084 13194139533864 true] [17592186262083 1089 "q-96987" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262083 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186262083 1100 "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nI. - ${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y=2x,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(1)=3$\nII. - $x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}=9y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(0)=1,\\,{y}^{''}(0)=2$\nIII. - $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y},\\,y(0)=1$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262083 1113 #uuid "8ed0d022-e8a6-5277-8016-371d657756f9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262083 1145 "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{'}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y=2x$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(1)=3.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\n- System II is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation $x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}=9y$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(0)=1,$ and ${y}^{''}(0)=2.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\n- System III is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y}$ together with the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262085 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262086 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262087 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262088 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262089 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262090 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262091 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262092 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186262084 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262089 13194139533864 true] [1759218626208